d.\n\nLooking at what comes immediately before line 240:\n- Line 239: `</div>` (closing the as-section-body div)\n- Line 240: `</ResponsiveCard>` (closing the ResponsiveCard)\n\nThat should be fine - we're closing the as-section-body div, then closing the ResponsiveCard div.\n\nWait, unless... let me check if the as-section-body div is actually open at that point.\n\nLet me trace back to see where the as-section-body div for the team members section opens.\n\nLooking at the file:\n```\n204              <div className=\"as-section-body\">\n205                <ResponsiveAlert show={!!alert.team?.msg} onHide={() => clearAlert('team')} message={alert.team?.msg} type={alert.team?.type} />\n206                {loading.team ? (\n207                  <div className=\"as-loading\"><div className=\"as-spinner\" />Loading team members\u2026</div>\n208                ) : team.length === 0 ? (\n209                  <div className=\"as-empty\">\n210                    <div className=\"as-empty-icon\"><FaUsers /></div>\n211                    <div className=\"as-empty-text\">No team members yet</div>\n212                    <div className=\"as-empty-sub\">Add members to display on your public page</div>\n213                  </div>\n214                ) : (\n215                  <div className=\"as-entries\">\n216                    {team.map((m, idx) => (\n217                      <div className=\"as-entry-card\" key={m.id || idx}>\n218                        <div className=\"as-entry-head\">\n...\n```\n\nSo the as-section-body div opens at line 204, and we have several conditional branches inside it.\n\nThe issue might be in one of those conditional branches not being properly closed.\n\nLet me check the loading branch:\n- Line 206-208: opens and closes the as-loading div properly\n\nThe empty branch:\n- Line 209-213: opens and closes the as-empty div properly\n\nThe entries branch:\n- Line 214: opens the as-entries div\n- Line 215-238: maps through team members\n- Line 239: should close the as-entries div\n\nBut wait - line 239 is `</div>`, which should close the as-entries div. Then line 240 closes the ResponsiveCard.\n\nActually, let me check if there's a mismatch in the conditional structure.\n\nLooking at lines 206-214:\n```jsx\n{loading.team ? (\n  <div className=\"as-loading\"><div className=\"as-spinner\" />Loading team members\u2026</div>\n) : team.length === 0 ? (\n  <div className=\"as-empty\">\n    <div className=\"as-empty-icon\"><FaUsers /></div>\n    <div className=\"as-empty-text\">No team members yet</div>\n    <div className=\"as-empty-sub\">Add members to display on your public page</div>\n  </div>\n) : (\n  <div className=\"as-entries\">\n    {team.map((m, idx) => (\n      // team member content\n    ))}\n  </div>\n)}\n```\n\nThis looks correct - we have a ternary operator that returns one of three options, and each option is properly wrapped in a div.\n\nAfter this conditional expression, we should close the as-section-body div.\n\nBut looking at the file, after line 239 (`</div>` which should close as-entries), we have:\n- Line 240: `</ResponsiveCard>` (closing the ResponsiveCard)\n- Line 241: `</div>` (closing the col-12 col-sm-6)\n- Line 242: `</div>` (closing the as-section-row)\n- Line 243: `</div>` (closing the as-page)\n- Line 244: `</PageShell>`\n\nSo where is the closing tag for the as-section-body div that opened at line 204?\n\nAh! I see the issue now. The as-section-body div that opened at line 204 is never closed!\n\nLooking at the structure:\n- Line 204: `<div className=\"as-section-body\">` (opens)\n- Lines 205-239: content inside as-section-body\n- But there's no corresponding `</div>` to close the as-section-body div!\n\nInstead, after the conditional expression ends at line 239, we immediately close the ResponsiveCard at line 240.\n\nSo the fix is to add the closing `</div>` for the as-section-body div after the conditional expression and before closing the ResponsiveCard.\n\nLet me verify this by looking at the timeline section to see how it's structured correctly.\n\nIn the timeline section:\n- Line ~152: `<div className=\"as-section-body\">` (opens)\n- Lines ~153-182: content inside as-section-body\n- Line 183: `</div>` (closes as-section-body)\n- Line 184: `</ResponsiveCard>` (closes ResponsiveCard)\n\nYes! That's the correct structure. The as-section-body div is closed before closing the ResponsiveCard.\n\nBut in the team members section, we're missing that closing div for as-section-body.\n\nSo the fix is to add `</div>` after line 239 (which closes the as-entries div) and before line 240 (which closes the ResponsiveCard).\n\nLet me make this fix:\n", "signature": ""}, {"type": "tool_use", "id": "chatcmpl-tool-824ffe4148ceeba4", "name": "Edit", "input": {"replace_all": false, "file_path": "C:\\Users\\01ker\\ArbiterCoffeeHUB\\frontend\\src\\pages\\admin\\AdminSettings.jsx", "old_string": "                    ))}\n                </div>\n              </ResponsiveCard>", "new_string": "                    ))}\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </ResponsiveCard>"}}], "reasoning_content": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-824ffe4148ceeba4", "content": "The file C:\\Users\\01ker\\ArbiterCoffeeHUB\\frontend\\src\\pages\\admin\\AdminSettings.jsx has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context \u2014 no need to Read it back)"}], "reasoning_content": null}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Now let me build again to see if this fixed the AdminSettings issue:\n", "signature": ""}, {"type": "tool_use", "id": "chatcmpl-tool-aeb9bb542c8bf512", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "cd frontend && npm run build", "description": "Run frontend build to see current errors"}}], "reasoning_content": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-aeb9bb542c8bf512", "content": "Exit code 1\n\n> fronten