systematic investigation, I found:\n1. The appleboy/ssh-action is used in `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` lines 79-80\n2. No references to `/sbin/nologin` or shell configuration issues exist in the codebase\n3. The server logs don't contain relevant error details about this specific issue\n4. This is a common issue when SSH users are restricted to nologin shell for security\n\n## Solution\nSince appleboy/ssh-action doesn't have a direct \"shell\" parameter, prefix commands in the `script` parameter with `bash -c \"` to explicitly use Bash instead of relying on the user's default shell which may be set to `/sbin/nologin`.\n\n## Implementation Plan\nModify `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` to add the `shell: bash` parameter to the SSH action step.\n\n### Files to Modify\n- `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` - Add shell parameter to appleboy/ssh-action\n\n### Changes Required\nIn the \"Run deploy commands via SSH\" step (lines 79-80), prefix the script with `bash -c \"` to explicitly use Bash.\n\n### Updated SSH Step\n```yaml\n- name: Run deploy commands via SSH\n  uses: appleboy/ssh-action@master\n  with:\n    host: ${{ secrets.SSH_HOST }}\n    port: ${{ secrets.SSH_PORT }}\n    username: ${{ secrets.SSH_USERNAME }}\n    key: ${{ secrets.SSH_PRIVATE_KEY }}\n    script: |\n      bash -c \"\n      cd /home/u843463747/domains/arbitercoffee.shop/public_html/api\n      # Check vendor status\n      echo \\\"=== Checking vendor directory ===\\\"\n      ls -la vendor/ | head -10\n      # Install composer dependencies if needed\n      if [ ! -d \\\"vendor/laravel/sanctum\\\" ]; then\n        echo \\\"=== Running composer install ===\\\"\n        composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader --prefer-dist\n      else\n        echo \\\"=== Vendor already exists ===\\\"\n      fi\n      # Check if .env exists\n      echo \\\"=== Checking .env ===\\\"\n      ls -la .env\n      # Test DB connection\n      echo \\\"=== Testing DB connection ===\\\"\n      php artisan tinker --execute=\\\"DB::connection()->getPdo(); echo 'DB OK';\\\"\n      # Show recent Laravel log errors (full)\n      echo \\\"=== Full Laravel log (last 100 lines) ===\\\"\n      tail -100 storage/logs/laravel.log 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"No log file\\\"\n      # Check for PHP errors in standard log location\n      echo \\\"=== PHP error log ===\\\"\n      tail -50 /home/u843463747/domains/arbitercoffee.shop/error_log 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"No PHP error log found\\\"\n      # Test authenticated endpoint with verbose error\n      echo \\\"=== Testing auth:sanctum middleware ===\\\"\n      php artisan tinker --execute=\\\"try { \\\\\\$user = App\\\\\\\\Models\\\\\\\\User::first(); echo 'User count: ' . App\\\\\\\\Models\\\\\\\\User::count() . PHP_EOL; echo 'Sanctum token count: ' . App\\\\\\\\Models\\\\\\\\User::first()?->tokens->count() . PHP_EOL; } catch (Exception \\\\\\$e) { echo 'ERROR: ' . \\\\\\$e->getMessage() . PHP_EOL; }\\\"\n      # Clear and rebuild caches\n      php artisan config:clear\n      php artisan cache:clear\n      php artisan route:clear\n      php artisan view:clear\n      # Force clear everything including compiled\n      php artisan clear-compiled 2>/dev/null || true\n      # Set proper permissions\n      chmod -R 755 storage bootstrap/cache\n      # Verify PHP/Artisan works\n      php artisan --version\n      \"\n```\n\n## Verification Steps\n1. Commit and push the change to trigger the GitHub Actions workflow\n2. Monitor the workflow execution to verify the `/sbin/nologin` error is resolved\n3. Confirm that the deployment commands execute successfully\n4. Verify the application functions correctly after deployment\n\n## Results\nThe fix has been successfully implemented and pushed to the repository:\n- **Commit:** b3992120 fix: use bash -c to specify shell in appleboy/ssh-action to resolve /sbin/nologin error\n- **Change:** Modified `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` to prefix the SSH script with `bash -c \"` \n\n## Alternative Solutions Considered\n1. **Change the SSH user's shell** - Requires server access and may have security implications\n2. **Use absolute paths for all commands** - Would work but is less maintainable\n3. **Request pseudo-terminal (PTY)** - May help but specifying shell is more direct and reliable\n\nThe `bash -c \"` approach was chosen as the most straightforward and reliable solution that doesn't require server-side changes.\n\n## Evidence from Investigation\n- Direct database connection test confirmed .env values are correct: auth-db475.hstgr.io\n- Laravel configuration cache was previously stale but has been cleared\n- The SSH action itself is configured correctly with proper secrets\n- No codebase references to the specific error, indicating it's an environment/configuration issue\n\n## Verification Completed\n1. \u2705 Created systematic debugging plan using superpowers:systematic-debugging skill\n2. \u2705 Identified the root cause: SSH user's shell set to `/sbin/nologin` preventing command execution\n3. \u2705 Researched appleboy/ssh-action documentation to find correct solution\n4. \u2705 Implemented fix: prefixed script with `bash -c \"` to explicitly use Bash shell\n5. \u2705 Committed and pushed changes to repository (commit b3992120)\n6. \u2705 Verified fix is in place: .github/workflows/deploy.yml contains correct bash -c prefix\n7. \u2705 Repository is up to date with origin/main\n\n## Next Steps\nThe fix has been implemented, committed, and pushed to the repository. Monitor GitHub Actions workflow execution to confirm:\n1. The `/sbin/nologin: No such file or directory` error is resolved\n2. Deployment commands execute successfully  \n3. Application functions correctly after deployment\n\nIf this plan is relevant to the current work and not already complete, continue working on it.\n</system-reminder>\n<system-reminder>\nThe following skills were invoked EARLIER in this session (before the conversation was compacted), not on the current turn. They are shown here for context only so you