36: `{m.bio ? ( ... ) : null}`\\n- Line 237: `</div>` (closing the as-entry-body div)\\n- Line 238: `}}` (closing two braces - likely the map function and the team array mapping)\\n- Line 239: `</div>` (closing the as-entries div)\\n- Line 240: `</ResponsiveCard>` (closing the ResponsiveCard)\\n- etc.\\n\\nThe problem is that the conditional rendering `{m.bio ? ( ... ) : null}` is returning either a div or null, which is fine, but the way it\\'s structured is causing JSX parsing issues.\\n\\nLet me look at a bit more context to understand the structure:\\n', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a488b10cc1cfe24c', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'Read', 'arguments': '{\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\01ker\\\\\\\\ArbiterCoffeeHUB\\\\\\\\frontend\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\pages\\\\\\\\admin\\\\\\\\AdminSettings.jsx\", \"offset\": 225, \"limit\": 20}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a488b10cc1cfe24c', 'content': '225\\t                            {m.role && <span style={{ fontWeight: 400, color: \\'#9ca3af\\', marginLeft: \\'.4rem\\', fontSize: \\'.8rem\\' }}>\u2014 {m.role}</span>}\\n226\\t                          </span>\\n227\\t                          <div className=\"as-entry-actions\">\\n228\\t                            <button className=\"as-icon-btn\" title=\"Edit\" onClick={() => openTmEdit(m)}><FaEdit /></button>\\n229\\t                            <button className=\"as-icon-btn danger\" title=\"Remove\" onClick={() => deleteTm(m)}><FaTrash /></button>\\n230\\t                          </div>\\n231\\t                        </div>\\n232\\t                        {m.bio ? (\\n233\\t                          <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\\n234\\t                            <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: \\'.875rem\\', color: \\'#6b7280\\' }}>{m.bio}</p>\\n235\\t                          </div>\\n236\\t                        ) : null}\\n237\\t                      </div>\\n238\\t                    ))}\\n239\\t            