{"time": "2026-05-24 17:15:28.430873+08:00", "level": "INFO", "message": "TRACE api.request.received", "module": "core.trace", "function": "trace_event", "line": 60, "request_id": "req_db92c3022db9", "http_method": "POST", "http_path": "/v1/messages", "stage": "ingress", "event": "api.request.received", "source": "api", "message_count": 124, "snapshot": {"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# currentDate\nToday's date is 2026-05-24.\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n\n"}, {"type": "text", "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement mobile-first responsive UI/UX refactor for all non-admin pages (Public, Barista, Kitchen, Customer) using existing responsive component library and Brand Identity Guidelines, following the plan in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-23-mobile-first-non-admin-refactor.md. Replace react-bootstrap components with custom responsive equivalents while maintaining functionality and improving mobile experience.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Mobile-first responsive design with CSS Flexbox/Grid\n   - Reusable responsive component library (Button, Card, Table, Form, Modal)\n   - Brand Identity Guidelines design tokens for spacing, typography, colors\n   - Standardized import paths using @/components/responsive/ alias\n   - Component variants (primary, secondary, danger, outline-*, success, info, warning)\n   - Responsive layout system (Container, Row, Col) with breakpoint classes\n   - Touch target optimization (minimum 48x48px)\n   - JSX syntax correction and proper component nesting\n\n3. Files and Code Sections Examined/Modified:\n   - frontend/src/pages/admin/AdminSettings.jsx: Fixed JSX structure errors with prematurely closed div tags\n   - frontend/src/pages/auth/ForgotPasswordPage.jsx: Added missing ResponsiveContainer closing tag\n   - frontend/src/pages/auth/LoginPage.jsx: Added missing ResponsiveForm closing tag\n   - frontend/src/pages/auth/RegisterPage.jsx: Added missing ResponsiveForm closing tag\n   - frontend/src/pages/auth/ResetPasswordPage.jsx: Added missing ResponsiveForm closing tag\n   - frontend/src/pages/barista/CompletedOrders.jsx: Added missing ResponsiveContainer wrapper\n   - frontend/src/pages/barista/PosPage.jsx: Fixed unterminated regular expression\n   - frontend/src/pages/barista/TrainingInsights.jsx: Fixed ResponsiveCol prop values\n   - frontend/src/pages/barista/components/OrderCard.jsx: Added missing closing div tags\n   - frontend/src/pages/customer/*.jsx: Fixed missing imports (Container, Row, Col, ResponsiveButton, etc.)\n   - frontend/src/pages/kitchen/*.jsx: Fixed missing imports for responsive components\n   - frontend/src/pages/notifications/*.jsx: Fixed Container import issues\n   - frontend/src/pages/public/*.jsx: Fixed various import and JSX syntax errors\n\n4. Errors and Fixes:\n   - JSX \"Adjacent JSX elements\" error in AdminSettings.jsx: Fixed by correcting div nesting structure (removed premature closing tags)\n   - \"Expected corresponding JSX closing tag\" errors: Added missing closing tags for ResponsiveContainer, ResponsiveForm components\n   - \"Unterminated regular expression\" in PosPage.jsx: Fixed extra closing parenthesis\n   - \"JSX value should be expression\" in TrainingInsights.jsx: Fixed ResponsiveCol prop syntax (md=6 lg=3 \u2192 md=\"6\" lg=\"3\")\n   - Missing import errors: Added proper imports for Container, Row, Col, ResponsiveButton, Spinner, Modal, etc. from @/components/responsive/\n   - Duplicate import issues: Corrected incorrect imports like ResponsiveResponsiveSpinner \u2192 ResponsiveSpinner\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Systematically identified and fixed JSX syntax errors preventing successful build\n   - Corrected import path issues by ensuring consistent use of @/components/responsive/ aliases\n   - Validated fixes by attempting rebuilds and tracking error reduction\n   - Maintained existing functionality while improving mobile responsiveness\n   - Verified component library usage consistency across all refactored pages\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial request to implement mobile-first refactor for admin and non-admin pages\n   - Multiple \"/superpowers:using-superpowers continue\" commands to continue development\n   - Reference to non-admin refactor plan documentation\n   - Explicit request to \"Continue the remaining tasks\":\n     * Task 8: Update Import Paths and Fix Any Broken References (fix JSX syntax errors, import issues)\n     * Task 9: Final Testing and Validation (test responsiveness, touch targets, visual consistency)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Task 8: Update Import Paths and Fix Any Broken References\n         - Fix remaining JSX syntax errors in identified files\n         - Ensure all component imports use correct @/components/responsive/ aliases\n         - Achieve successful build with npm run build --prefix frontend\n   - Task 9: Final Testing and Validation\n         - Test responsive behavior at breakpoints (320px, 480px, 768px)\n         - Verify all touch targets \u226548x48px\n         - Validate visual consistency with Brand Identity Guidelines\n         - Test all refactored pages for proper functionality\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, work was focused on resolving remaining JSX syntax errors to enable a successful build. Specific issues being addressed:\n   - AdminSettings.jsx: Adjacent JSX elements error (line 240:14)\n   - RegisterPage.jsx: Missing ResponsiveContainer closing tag (line 383:8)\n   - ResetPasswordPage.jsx: Missing ResponsiveContainer clo