div>\n      </PageShell>\n```\n\nActually, let me look at the full team section to see the structure:\n\nFrom line 188:\n```\n          {/* \u2500\u2500 Team Members \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */}\n          <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">\n            <ResponsiveCard className=\"as-section-card\">\n              <div className=\"as-section-head\">\n                ...\n              </div>\n              <div className=\"as-section-body\">\n                ...\n                {loading.team ? (\n                  <div className=\"as-loading\">...</div>\n                ) : team.length === 0 ? (\n                  <div className=\"as-empty\">...</div>\n                ) : (\n                  <div className=\"as-entries\">\n                    {team.map((m, idx) => (\n                      <div className=\"as-entry-card\" key={m.id || idx}>\n                        <div className=\"as-entry-head\">\n                          ...\n                        </div>\n                        {m.bio && (\n                          <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n                            <p>{m.bio}</p>\n                          </div>\n                        )}\n                      </div>\n                    ))}\n                  </div>\n                )}\n              </div>\n            </ResponsiveCard>\n          </div>\n```\n\nI think I see the issue! Looking at the bio conditional rendering:\n\n```jsx\n{m.bio && (\n  <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n    <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: '.875rem', color: '#6b7280' }}>{m.bio}</p>\n  </div>\n)}\n```\n\nWhen m.bio is falsy, this expression evaluates to false (a boolean false), not null or undefined. In JSX, false is a valid valu