      <ResponsiveCard className=\"as-section-card\">\n            ...\n          </ResponsiveCard>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </PageShell>\n);\n```\n\nThis structure looks correct - there's only one root element (the div with className=\"as-page\") inside the PageShell.\n\nWait, let me look at the actual error line again. The error says line 240:14. Let me see what's at that exact position.\n\nLooking at the end of the file:\n```\n230                          </div>\n231                        </div>\n232                        {m.bio && (\n233                          <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n234                            <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: '.875rem', color: '#6b7280' }}>{m.bio}</p>\n235                          </div>\n236                        )}\n237                      </div>\n238                    ))}\n239                </div>\n240              </ResponsiveCard>\n241            </div>\n242          </div>\n243        </div>\n244      </PageShell>\n245  );\n246};\n```\n\nLine 240 is `</ResponsiveCard>`. The error says \"Adjacent JSX elements must be wrapped in an enclosing tag\" at this position.\n\nThis suggests that at line 240, there are two JSX elements sitting next to each other. But looking at the structure, line 239 is `</div>` (closing the as-section-body), line 240 is `</ResponsiveCard>` (closing the ResponsiveCard), line 241 is `</div>` (closing the col-12 col-sm-6), etc.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The error might be indicating that there's a missing opening tag somewhere, causing the parser to see adjacent elements when it shouldn't.\n\nLet me look at the team member section structure more carefully. Starting from line 188:\n\n```jsx\n          {/* \u2500\u2500 Team Members \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\