issue is that we have a closing parenthesis and curly brace followed by a closing ResponsiveCard tag, which suggests that we\\'re missing an opening tag or have extra closing tags.\\n\\nLooking at lines 230-240:\\n```\\n                        {m.bio && (\\n                          <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\\n                            <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: \\'.875rem\\', color: \\'#6b7280\\' }}>{m.bio}</p>\\n                          </div>\\n                        )}\\n                      </div>\\n                    ))}\\n                  </div>\\n                </ResponsiveCard>\\n```\\n\\nLet me trace the opening tags:\\n- Line 232: `<div className=\"as-entry-body\">` (opened conditionally)\\n- Line 236: `</div>` (closes the as-entry-body)\\n- Line 230: `<div className=\"as-entry-actions\">`\\n- Line 231: `</div>` (closes as-entry-actions) - Wait, I don\\'t see this!\\n\\nAh, here\\'s the issue! We\\'re missing the closing tag for the as-entry-actions div. Let me add it.\\n\\nActually, looking again:\\nLine 227: `<div className=\"as-entry-actions\">`\\nLine 230 should be the closing tag for this div, but it\\'s missing.\\n\\nSo we need to add `</div>` before the closing of the as-entry-head div.\\n\\nLet me fix this:\\n', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-828eb537ce4953fc', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'Edit', 'arguments': '{\"replace_all\": false, \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\01ker\\\\\\\\ArbiterCoffeeHUB\\\\\\\\frontend\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\pages\\\\\\\\admin\\\\\\\\AdminSettings.jsx\", \"old_string\": \"                          <div className=\\\\\"as-entry-actions\\\\\">\\\\n                            <button className=\\\\\"as-icon-btn\\\\\" title=\\\\\"Edit\\\\\" onClick={() => openTmEdit(m)}><FaEdit /></button>\\\\n                            <button className=\\\\\"as-icon-btn danger\\\\\" title=\\\\\"Remove\\\\\" onClick={() => deleteTm(m)}><FaTrash /></button>\\\\n                          </div>\\\\n