node, and the elements after false).\n\nThe fix is to either:\n1. Use a ternary operator that returns null when false: `{m.bio ? (<div>...</div>) : null}`\n2. Wrap the whole thing in a way that prevents adjacent elements\n\nLet me check if this is indeed the issue by looking at the exact structure around the bio rendering.\n\nActually, let me look at the timeline section to see how it handles the description rendering, since that looks similar:\n\nIn the timeline section (around line 175):\n```jsx\n{item.description && (\n  <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n    <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: '.875rem', color: '#6b7280' }}>{item.description}</p>\n  </div>\n)}\n```\n\nThis has the same pattern! So both sections have this issue.\n\nBut wait, the error is pointing to line 240:14, which is in the team section. Let me see what's at that exact position.\n\nLet me get a more precise view of the file around line 240:\n", "tool_calls": [{"id": "chatcmpl-tool-bace5f58d73388d8", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\01ker\\\\ArbiterCoffeeHUB\\\\frontend\\\\src\\\\pages\\\\admin\\\\AdminSettings.jsx\", \"offset\": 235, \"limit\": 15}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bace5f58d73388d8", "content": "235\t                          </div>\n236\t                        ) : null}\n237\t                      </div>\n238\t                    ))}\n239\t                </div>\n240\t              </ResponsiveCard>\n241\t          </div>\n242\t        </div>\n243\t      </div>\n244\t    </PageShell>\n245\t  );\n246\t};\n247\t\n248\texport default AdminSettings;\n249\t"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "reasoning_content": "Let me look at the AdminSettings.jsx file more carefully around line 240 where the error is occurring. The error says \"Adjacent JSX elements must be wrapped in an enclosing tag\" at line 240:14.\n\nLooking at the end of the file:\n```\n235                          </div>\n236          