cent div elements at the same level (inside the as-section-row). And that is the problem!\n\nWe have:\n\n        <div className=\"as-section-row row g-4\">\n          {/* Timeline column */}\n          <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">   <!-- opened at line 135 -->\n            ... timeline card ...\n          </div>   <!-- closed at line 186 -->\n          {/* Team column -->  \n          <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">   <!-- opened at line 189 -->\n            ... team card ...\n          </div>   <!-- closed at line 241 -->\n        </div>\n\nBut wait, that is actually two div elements (the two columns) that are siblings. And that is allowed because they are both children of the as-section-row div. However, note that the error is about adjacent JSX elements. In JSX, you can have multiple siblings as long as they are all wrapped in a single parent. Here, the two columns are both children of the as-section-row div, so they are siblings and that is allowed.\n\nBut the error says adjacent JSX elements must be wrapped in an enclosing tag. This error would occur if we had, for example, two elements at the same level without a parent. In this case, the two columns have a parent (the as-section-row div). So why the error?\n\nWait, note that the as-section-row div is opened at line 133 and closed at line 242. So the structure is:\n\n<div className=\"as-section-row row g-4\">\n  <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\"> ... </div>\n  <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\"> ... </div>\n</div>\n\nThat is valid.\n\nHowever, let's look at the exact lines again. I suspect that there might be a missing closing tag for the timeline column's div? But we see it at line 186.\n\nAlternatively, note that the timeline section's ResponsiveCard is closed at line 185, and then we have:\n\n186:          </div>   <!-- This closes the timeline column div -->\n187:          {/* \u2500\u2500 Team Members \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2