s the as-page div -->\n244:    </PageShell>   <!-- This closes the PageShell -->\n\nSo the structure seems correct.\n\nBut wait, the error is at line 240:14, which is the closing tag of the ResponsiveCard inside the team column. The error says \"Adjacent JSX elements must be wrapped in an enclosing tag\". This error is being triggered by the ResponsiveCard's closing tag? That doesn't make sense.\n\nPerhaps the issue is that inside the team column's ResponsiveCard, we have adjacent JSX elements? Let's look at the content of the team column's ResponsiveCard.\n\nWe have:\n\n190:            <ResponsiveCard className=\"as-section-card\">\n191:              <div className=\"as-section-head\">\n... \n203:              </div>\n204:              <div className=\"as-section-body\">\n205:                <ResponsiveAlert ... />\n206:                {loading.team ? (...) : team.length === 0 ? (...) : (\n207:                  <div className=\"as-entries\">\n208:                    {team.map((m, idx) => (\n209:                      <div className=\"as-entry-card\" key={m.id || idx}>\n210:                        <div className=\"as-entry-head\">\n... \n230:                        {m.bio && (\n231:                          <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n... \n236:                        )}\n237:                      </div>\n238:                    ))}\n239:                  </div>\n240:                )}\n241:              </div>\n242:            </ResponsiveCard>\n\nWait, note that at line 206, we have:\n\n                {loading.team ? (\n                  <div className=\"as-loading\">...</div>\n                ) : team.length === 0 ? (\n                  <div className=\"as-empty\">...</div>\n                ) : (\n                  <div className=\"as-entries\">\n                    {team.map(...)}\n                  </div>\n                )}\n\nThis is a ternary expression that returns JSX. However, note that the ternary expression is not wrapped in a div or fragment. But that is allowed because it is a single expression that returns one of three possible JSX elements.\n\nBut wait, the error is at line 240, which is the closing tag of the ResponsiveCard. Let me look at the lines around 240:\n\n239:                  </div>   <!-- This closes the as-entries div -->\n240:                )}        <!-- This closes the ternary expression and the as-section-body div? -->\n\nActually, note that the as-section-body div is opened at line 204 and then we have the ternary expression. The ternary expression returns either the loading div, the empty div, or the as-entries div. Then we close the as-section-body div at line 241? Let's see:\n\n204:              <div className=\"as-section-body\">\n205:                <ResponsiveAlert ... />\n206:                {loading.team ? (...) : team.length === 0 ? (...) : (...) }\n207:              </div>   <!-- This is line 241? -->\n\nWait, we have to count the lines. Let me try to reconstruct the team member section from the file we have.\n\nAlternatively, note that the error might be because we have two adjacent elements in the as-section-body: the ResponsiveAlert and the ternary expression. But that is not allowed because they are two siblings without a wrapper.\n\nLook at lines 204-207:\n\n              <div className=\"as-section-body\">\n                <ResponsiveAlert show={!!alert.team?.msg} onHide={() => clearAlert('team')} message={alert.team?.msg} type={alert.team?.type} />\n                {loading.team ? (...) : team.length === 0 ? (...) : (...) }\n              </div>\n\nHere, inside the as-section-body div, we have two elements:\n1. <ResponsiveAlert ... />\n2. {loading.team ? (...) : team.length === 0 ? (...) : (...) }\n\nThese are two adjacent JSX elements (a component and a ternary expression that returns JSX) without being wrapped in a single parent. That is the cause of the error!\n\nWe must wrap the contents of the as-section-body div in a single parent, or use a fragment, or put them