n132\t      <div className=\"as-page\">\n133\t        <div className=\"as-section-row row g-4\">\n134\t          {/* \u2500\u2500 Company Timeline \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */}\n135\t          <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">\n136\t            <ResponsiveCard className=\"as-section-card\">\n...\n244\t    </PageShell>\n245\t  );\n246\t};\n247\t\n248\texport default AdminSettings;\n```\n\nThis looks correct - the PageShell opens at line 131 and closes at line 244.\n\nWait, I think I might have it. Let me check if there are any stray characters or content outside the JSX.\n\nActually, let me try a simpler approach. Since the error is specifically about adjacent JSX elements, and it's pointing to line 240, let me see if wrapping the content in a React fragment fixes it, and then we can work backwards.\n\nBut first, let me check if the issue is in the timeline section instead and the error is misleading.\n\nLet me look at the timeline section ending:\n\nAround lines 180-187:\n```\n180\t                        )}\n181\t                      </div>\n182\t                    ))}\n183\t                  </div>\n184\t                )}\n185              </ResponsiveCard>\n186            </div>\n187\n188\t          {/* \u2500\u2500 Team Members \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */}\n```\n\nThis looks correct too.\n\nLet me try to fix this by ensuring that we have proper nesting. Maybe the issue is that we're missing a wrapper around the two columns.\n\nActually, in Bootstrap, when you use columns, they should be wrapped in a row, which they are (line 133: `<div className=\"as-section-row row g-4\">`). And that row should be wrapped in a container, which it is (line 132: `<div className=\"as-page\">`).\n\nBut let me check if the as-page div is actually needed or if it's causing issues.\n\nLet me try removing the as-page div and see if that helps, or alternatively, let me try wrapping the two columns in an additional div to make sure there's only one child of the row.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the error: \"Adjacent JSX elements must be wrapped in an enclosing tag. Did you want a JSX fragment <>...</>?\"\n\nThis error occurs when you have something like:\n```jsx\nreturn (\n  <div>Element 1</div>\n  <div>Element 2</div>\n);\n```\n\nInstead of:\n```jsx\nreturn (\n  <div>\n    <div>Element 1</div>\n    <div>Element 2</div>\n  </div>\n);\n```\n\nOr using fragments:\n```jsx\nreturn (\n  <>\n    <div>Element 1</div>\n    <div>Element 2</div>\n  </>\n);\n```\n\nSo the error suggests that at the location of the error, there are two sibling JSX elements that aren't wrapped in a common parent.\n\nGiven that the error is at line 240 (the `</ResponsiveCard>`), let me see what JSX elements are adjacent around there.\n\nActually, let me think about when this error typically occurs. It often happens when you have a conditional that returns JSX incorrectly, or when you're mapping and accidentally return adjacent elements.\n\nLet me look again at the team member mapping section:\n\n```jsx\n{team.map((m, idx) => (\n  <div className=\"as-entry-card\" key={m.id || idx}>\n    ...\n  </div>\n))}\n```\n\nThis should be fine - the map function returns a single JSX element (the div) for each item.\n\nWait, unless... what if there's an issue with the parentheses? Let me check the exact structure:\n\n```jsx\n{team.map((m, idx) => (\n  <div className=\"as-entry-card\" key={m.id || idx}>\n    <div className=\"as-entry-head\">\n      ...\n    </div>\n    {m.bio && (\n      <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n        <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: '.875rem', color: '#6b7280' }}>{m.bio}</p>\n      </div>\n    )}\n  </div>\n))}\n```\n\nLooking at this, I see a potential issue! The `{m.bio && (...)}` is inside the `as-entry-card` div, which is correct. But let me check if the parentheses are balanced.\n\nWe have:\n- `team.map((m, idx) => (` - opens map arrow function\n- `<div className=\"as-entry-card\" key={m.id || idx}>` - opens entry card div\n- `<div className=\"as-entry-head\">` - opens entry head\n- ... head content ...\n- `</div>` - closes entry head\n- `{m.bio && (` - opens bio condition\n- `<div className=\"as-entry-body\">` - opens entry body\n- `<p>...</p>` - paragraph\n- `</div>` - closes entry body\n- `)}` - closes bio condition AND map arrow function\n- `</div>` - closes entry card div\n- `))` - closes map function\n\nWait, that looks wrong! We have `)}` followed by `</div>` followed by `))`.\n\nLet me retrace:\n1. `team.map((m, idx) => (` - opens map arrow function (expects closing `)`)\n2. `<div className=\"as-entry-card\" key={m.id || idx}>` - opens div\n3. `<div className=\"as-entry-head\">` - opens head div\n4. ... head content ...\n5. `</div>` - closes head div\n6. `{m.bio && (` - opens bio condition (expects closing `)`)\n7. `<div className=\"as-entry-body\">` - opens body div\n8. `<p>...</p>` - paragraph\n9. `</div>` - closes body div\n10. `)` - closes bio condition\n11. `</div>` - closes entry card div\n12. `)` - closes map arrow function\n13. `}` - closes the curly braces of the JSX expression\n\nSo we should have: `{team.map((m, idx) => ( ... ))}`\n\nWhich means after the entry card div closes, we should have `)` to close the map arrow function, then `}` to close the JSX braces.\n\nBut in the code at line 238, I see `)}` which would be closing the bio condition and then... what?\n\nLet me look at the actual lines again:\n```\n236                        )}\n237                      </div>\n238                    ))}\n239                </div>\n```\n\nLine 236: `)}` - this should be closing the bio condition\nLine 237: `</div>` - this should be closing the as-entry-body\nLine 238: `)}}` - this should be closing the map arrow function and the JSX expression\n\nActually, that looks correct:\n- Line 233: `{m.bio && (` - opens bio condition\n- Line 236: `)` - closes bio condition  \n- Line 237: `</div>` - closes as-entry-body div\n- Line 238: `)` - closes map arrow function\n- Line 238: `}` - closes JSX expression braces\n- Line 239: `</div>` - closes as-entries div\n\nWait, but line 238 shows `)}}` which is three characters: `)`, `}`, `}`. That would be:\n- `)` - closes map arrow function\n- `}` - closes JSX expression  \n- `}` - extra closing brace?\n\nLet me check what the actual text is. Looking back at the file content I showed earlier:\n\nLine 236: `)}`\nLine 237: `</div>`  \nLine 238: `)}`\n\nSo line 238 is `)}` - that's close parenthesis, close brace.\n\nThis would mean:\n- `)` closes the map arrow function\n- `}` closes the JSX expression\n\nBut then what closes the bio condition? Let me retrace from the bio condition opening:\n\nLine 232: `{m.bio && (` - opens bio condition\nWe need a matching `)` to close it.\n\nIf line 236 is `)}`:\n- `)` closes the bio condition\n- `}` closes... what? It should close the JSX expression for the map, but we still need to close the map arrow function.\n\nActually, let me write it out properly:\n\n```jsx\n{team.map((m, idx) => (  // <-- outer {\n  <div className=\"as-entry-card\" key={m.id || idx}>\n    ... \n    {m.bio && (           // <-- inner {\n      <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n        <p>{m.bio}</p>\n      </div>\n    )}                    // <-- inner } closes the bio condition && expression\n    ... \n  </div>\n)}                       // <-- outer ) closes the map arrow function, outer } closes the JSX expression\n```\n\nSo we should have:\n- Opening bio condition: `{m.bio && (`\n- Closing bio condition: `)`  \n- Closing map arrow function: `)`\n- Closing JSX expression: `}`\n\nThat would be `)}` for the bio condition close + map arrow function close, and then another `}` for the JSX expression close.\n\nSo we should see: `)}` followed by `}`.\n\nLooking at the file:\nLine 236: `)}`  (bio condition close + map arrow function close?)\nLine 237: `</div>`\nLine 238: `)}`  (what is this?)\n\nActually, let me look at the exact snippet from the file again:\n\n```\n230                          </div>\n231                        </div>\n232                        {m.bio && (\n233                          <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n234                            <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: '.875rem', color: '#6b7280' }}>{m.bio}</p>\n235                          </div>\n236                        )}\n237                      </div>\n238                    ))}\n239                </div>\n```\n\nSo:\n- Line 232: `{m.bio && (` \n- Line 236: `)}`  <- This closes the bio condition (`)`) and... what does the `}` close?\n- Line 237: `</div>` <- Closes the as-entry-body div\n- Line 238: `)}`  <- This should close the map arrow function (`)`) and the JSX expression (`}`)\n- Line 239: `</div>` <- Closes the as-entries div\n\nSo line 236's `}` is closing... let me see what JSX expression is open at that point.\n\nAt line 232, we open: `{m.bio && (`\nThis opens a JavaScript expression (the && condition) inside the JSX.\n\nThe corresponding closing should be just `)` to close the && expression, not `}`.\n\nAh! I think I found it!\n\nThe bio condition should be:\n```jsx\n{m.bio && (\n  <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n    <p>{m.bio}</p>\n  </div>\n)}\n```\n\nBut we have:\n```jsx\n{m.bio && (\n  <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n    <p>{m.bio}</p>\n  </div>\n)}\n```\n\nSo line 236 should be just `)` not `)}`.\n\nThe extra `}` is causing a problem - it's closing a JSX expression that isn't open, or it's creating an imbalance that leads to the adjacent elements error.\n\nLet me fix this:\n\nChange line 236 from `)}` to just `)`.\n\nLet me make that change:\n", "tool_calls": [{"id": "chatcmpl-tool-b6be373a5270878c", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Edit", "arguments": "{\"replace_all\": false, \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\01ker\\\\ArbiterCoffeeHUB\\\\frontend\\\\src\\\\pages\\\\admin\\\\AdminSettings.jsx\", \"old_string\": \"                        {m.bio && (\\n                          <div className=\\\"as-entry-body\\\">\\n                            <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: '.875rem', color: '#6b7280' }}>{m.bio}</p>\\n                          </div>\\n                        )}\", \"new_string\": \"                        {m.bio && (\\n                          <div className=\\\"as-entry-body\\\">\\n                            <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: '.875rem', color: '#6b7280' }}>{m.bio}</p>\\n                          </div>\\n                        )}\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b6be373a5270878c", "content": "<tool_use_error>No changes to make: old_string and new_string are exactly the same.</tool_use_error>"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "reasoning_content": "Let me approach this differently. The error is \"Adjacent JSX elements must be wrapped in an enclosing tag\" at line 240:14. Let me see what's actually at that location by examining the exact content around there.\n\nActually, let me just try a simpler approach. Since the error says we have adjacent JSX elements that need to be wrapped, let me look at the structure and see if I can spot where two elements are sitting next to each other without a common parent.\n\nLooking at the return statement, we have:\n```jsx\nreturn (\n  <PageShell ...>\n    <div className=\"as-page\">\n      <div className=\"as-section-row row g-4\">\n        {/* Timeline section */}\n        <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">\n          ... timeline card ...\n        </div>\n        \n        {/* Team section */}\n        <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">\n          ... team card ...\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </PageShell>\n```\n\nThis should be valid JSX. The two columns are siblings but they're both wrapped in the row div.\n\nWait, unless there's something wrong with the indentation or there are actually elements at the same level that I'm not seeing.\n\nLet me try to rewrite the entire return statement with proper formatting to see if I can spot the issue:\n", "tool_calls": [{"id": "chatcmpl-tool-b69c7e15a68b190d", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "Read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\01ker\\\\ArbiterCoffeeHUB\\\\frontend\\\\src\\\\pages\\\\admin\\\\AdminSettings.jsx\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b69c7e15a68b190d", "content": "1\timport React, { useEffect, useState, useCallback } from 'react';\n2\timport { ResponsiveButton, ResponsiveForm, ResponsiveModal, ResponsiveAlert, ResponsiveCard } from '@/components/responsive';\n3\timport {\n4\t  FaHistory, FaUsers, FaPlus, FaEdit, FaTrash, FaTimes,\n5\t  FaChevronUp, FaChevronDown, FaSave, FaUserCircle, FaSync,\n6\t} from 'react-icons/fa';\n7\timport apiService from '../../services/api.service';\n8\timport { API_ENDPOINTS } from '../../config/api';\n9\timport PageShell from '../../components/layout/PageShell';\n10\timport './AdminSettings.css';\n11\t\n12\t// \u2500\u2500\u2500 Blank helpers \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n13\tconst blankTimeline = () => ({ year: new Date().getFullYear(), title: '', description: '' });\n14\tconst blankMember   = () => ({ name: '', role: '', bio: '', photo_url: '', display_order: 0 });\n15\t\n16\t// \u2500\u2500\u2500 Alert banner \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n17\tconst Alert = ({ msg, type, onClose }) =>\n18\t  msg ? (\n19\t    <div className={`as-alert ${type}`}>\n20\t      {msg}\n21\t      <button className=\"as-alert-close\" onClick={onClose}><FaTimes /></button>\n22\t    </div>\n23\t  ) : null;\n24\t\n25\t// \u2500\u2500\u2500 Main Component \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n26\tconst AdminSettings = () => {\n27\t  const [timeline, setTimeline]   = useState([]);\n28\t  const [team, setTeam]           = useState([]);\n29\t  const [loading, setLoading]     = useState({ timeline: true, team: true });\n30\t  const [saving, setSaving]       = useState({ timeline: false, team: false });\n31\t  const [alert, setAlert]         = useState({ timeline: null, team: null });\n32\t  const [error, setError]         = useState(null);\n33\t\n34\t  // Modal state shared\n35\t  const [tlModal, setTlModal]     = useState(false);\n36\t  const [tmModal, setTmModal]     = useState(false);\n37\t  const [selected, setSelected]   = useState(null);\n38\t  const [tlForm, setTlForm]       = useState(blankTimeline());\n39\t  const [tmForm, setTmForm]       = useState(blankMember());\n40\t\n41\t  const clearAlert = (key) => setAlert(p => ({ ...p, [key]: null }));\n42\t  const showAlert = (key, msg, type = 'success') => {\n43\t    setAlert(p => ({ ...p, [key]: { msg, type } }));\n44\t    setTimeout(() => clearAlert(key), 4000);\n45\t  };\n46\t\n47\t  // \u2500\u2500 Fetch Timeline \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n48\t  const fetchTimeline = useCallback(async () => {\n49\t    setLoading(p => ({ ...p, timeline: true }));\n50\t    try {\n51\t      const res = await apiService.get(API_ENDPOINTS.ADMIN.SETTINGS.TIMELINE);\n52\t      if (res.success) setTimeline(Array.isArray(res.data) ? res.data : (res.data?.data || []));\n53\t    } catch { setError('Failed to load timeline.'); }\n54\t    finally { setLoading(p => ({ ...p, timeline: false })); }\n55\t  }, []);\n56\t\n57\t  // \u2500\u2500 Fetch Team \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n58\t  const fetchTeam = useCallback(async () => {\n59\t    setLoading(p => ({ ...p, team: true }));\n60\t    try {\n61\t      const res = await apiService.get(API_ENDPOINTS.ADMIN.SETTINGS.TEAM);\n62\t      if (res.success) setTeam(Array.isArray(res.data) ? res.data : (res.data?.data || []));\n63\t    } catch { setError('Failed to load team members.'); }\n64\t    finally { setLoading(p => ({ ...p, team: false })); }\n65\t  }, []);\n66\t\n67\t  useEffect(() => { fetchTimeline(); fetchTeam(); }, [fetchTimeline, fetchTeam]);\n68\t\n69\t  // \u2500\u2500 Timeline CRUD \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n70\t  const openTlAdd  = () => { setSelected(null); setTlForm(blankTimeline()); setTlModal(true); };\n71\t  const openTlEdit = (item) => { setSelected(item); setTlForm({ year: item.year || '', title: item.title || '', description: item.description || '' }); setTlModal(true); };\n72\t\n73\t  const saveTl = async (e) => {\n74\t    e.preventDefault();\n75\t    setSaving(p => ({ ...p, timeline: true }));\n76\t    try {\n77\t      const res = selected\n78\t        ? await apiService.put(`${API_ENDPOINTS.ADMIN.SETTINGS.TIMELINE}/${selected.id}`, tlForm)\n79\t        : await apiService.post(API_ENDPOINTS.ADMIN.SETTINGS.TIMELINE, tlForm);\n80\t      if (res.success) { setTlModal(false); fetchTimeline(); showAlert('timeline', selected ? 'Timeline entry updated.' : 'Timeline entry added.'); }\n81\t      else showAlert('timeline', res.message || 'Save failed.', 'danger');\n82\t    } catch { showAlert('timeline', 'Failed to save timeline entry.', 'danger'); }\n83\t    finally { setSaving(p => ({ ...p, timeline: false })); }\n84\t  };\n85\t\n86\t  const deleteTl = async (item) => {\n87\t    if (!window.confirm(`Delete \"${item.title}\" (${item.year})?`)) return;\n88\t    try {\n89\t      await apiService.delete(`${API_ENDPOINTS.ADMIN.SETTINGS.TIMELINE}/${item.id}`);\n90\t      fetchTimeline(); showAlert('timeline', 'Entry deleted.');\n91\t    } catch { showAlert('timeline', 'Delete failed.', 'danger'); }\n92\t  };\n93\t\n94\t  const moveTl = (idx, dir) => {\n95\t    const arr = [...timeline];\n96\t    const target = idx + dir;\n97\t    if (target < 0 || target >= arr.length) return;\n98\t    [arr[idx], arr[target]] = [arr[target], arr[idx]];\n99\t    setTimeline(arr);\n100\t  };\n101\t\n102\t  // \u2500\u2500 Team CRUD \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n103\t  const openTmAdd  = () => { setSelected(null); setTmForm(blankMember()); setTmModal(true); };\n104\t  const openTmEdit = (m) => { setSelected(m); setTmForm({ name: m.name || '', role: m.role || '', bio: m.bio || '', photo_url: m.photo_url || '', display_order: m.display_order || 0 }); setTmModal(true); };\n105\t\n106\t  const saveTm = async (e) => {\n107\t    e.preventDefault();\n108\t    setSaving(p => ({ ...p, team: true }));\n109\t    try {\n110\t      const res = selected\n111\t        ? await apiService.put(`${API_ENDPOINTS.ADMIN.SETTINGS.TEAM}/${selected.id}`, tmForm)\n112\t        : await apiService.post(API_ENDPOINTS.ADMIN.SETTINGS.TEAM, tmForm);\n113\t      if (res.success) { setTmModal(false); fetchTeam(); showAlert('team', selected ? 'Member updated.' : 'Member added.'); }\n114\t      else showAlert('team', res.message || 'Save failed.', 'danger');\n115\t    } catch { showAlert('team', 'Failed to save team member.', 'danger'); }\n116\t    finally { setSaving(p => ({ ...p, team: false })); }\n117\t  };\n118\t\n119\t  const deleteTm = async (m) => {\n120\t    if (!window.confirm(`Remove team member \"${m.name}\"?`)) return;\n121\t    try {\n122\t      await apiService.delete(`${API_ENDPOINTS.ADMIN.SETTINGS.TEAM}/${m.id}`);\n123\t      fetchTeam(); showAlert('team', 'Member removed.');\n124\t    } catch { showAlert('team', 'Delete failed.', 'danger'); }\n125\t  };\n126\t\n127\t  const tlField = k => ({ value: tlForm[k], onChange: e => setTlForm(p => ({ ...p, [k]: e.target.value })) });\n128\t  const tmField = k => ({ value: tmForm[k], onChange: e => setTmForm(p => ({ ...p, [k]: e.target.value })) });\n129\t\n130\t  return (\n131\t    <PageShell title=\"Settings\" subtitle=\"Manage company timeline and team members\" error={error} onRetry={() => { fetchTimeline(); fetchTeam(); }}>\n132\t      <div className=\"as-page\">\n133\t        <div className=\"as-section-row row g-4\">\n134\t          {/* \u2500\u2500 Company Timeline \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */}\n135\t          <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">\n136\t            <ResponsiveCard className=\"as-section-card\">\n137\t              <div className=\"as-section-head\">\n138\t                <div className=\"as-section-icon green\"><FaHistory /></div>\n139\t                <span className=\"as-section-title\">Company Timeline</span>\n140\t                <span className=\"as-section-count\">{timeline.length} entries</span>\n141\t                <div className=\"as-head-actions\">\n142\t                  <ResponsiveButton variant=\"outline-secondary\" size=\"sm\" className=\"as-btn add\" onClick={fetchTimeline} title=\"Refresh\">\n143\t                    <FaSync />\n144\t                  </ResponsiveButton>\n145\t                  <ResponsiveButton variant=\"primary\" size=\"sm\" className=\"as-btn add\" onClick={openTlAdd}>\n146\t                    <FaPlus />Add Entry\n147\t                  </ResponsiveButton>\n148\t                </div>\n149\t              </div>\n150\t              <div className=\"as-section-body\">\n151\t                <ResponsiveAlert show={!!alert.timeline?.msg} onHide={() => clearAlert('timeline')} message={alert.timeline?.msg} type={alert.timeline?.type} />\n152\t                {loading.timeline ? (\n153\t                  <div className=\"as-loading\"><div className=\"as-spinner\" />Loading timeline\u2026</div>\n154\t                ) : timeline.length === 0 ? (\n155\t                  <div className=\"as-empty\">\n156\t                    <div className=\"as-empty-icon\"><FaHistory /></div>\n157\t                    <div className=\"as-empty-text\">No timeline entries yet</div>\n158\t                    <div className=\"as-empty-sub\">Add your first milestone to showcase your journey</div>\n159\t                  </div>\n160\t                ) : (\n161\t                  <div className=\"as-entries\">\n162\t                    {timeline.map((item, idx) => (\n163\t                      <div className=\"as-entry-card\" key={item.id || idx}>\n164\t                        <div className=\"as-entry-head\">\n165\t                          <div className=\"as-entry-num\">{idx + 1}</div>\n166\t                          <span className=\"as-year-pill\">{item.year}</span>\n167\t                          <span className={`as-entry-title ${item.title ? '' : 'muted'}`}>{item.title || 'Untitled entry'}</span>\n168\t                          <div className=\"as-entry-actions\">\n169\t                            <button className=\"as-icon-btn\" title=\"Move up\"   disabled={idx === 0}                   onClick={() => moveTl(idx, -1)}><FaChevronUp /></button>\n170\t                            <button className=\"as-icon-btn\" title=\"Move down\" disabled={idx === timeline.length - 1} onClick={() => moveTl(idx, +1)}><FaChevronDown /></button>\n171\t                            <button className=\"as-icon-btn\" title=\"Edit\" onClick={() => openTlEdit(item)}><FaEdit /></button>\n172\t                            <button className=\"as-icon-btn danger\" title=\"Delete\" onClick={() => deleteTl(item)}><FaTrash /></button>\n173\t                          </div>\n174\t                        </div>\n175\t                        {item.description && (\n176\t                          <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\n177\t                            <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: '.875rem', color: '#6b7280' }}>{item.description}</p>\n178\t                          </div>\n179\t                        )}\n180\t                      </div>\n181\t                    ))}\n182\t                  </div>\n183\t                )}\n184\t              </div>\n185\t            </ResponsiveCard>\n186\t          </div>\n187\t\n188\t          {/* \u2500\u2500 Team Members \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */}\n189\t          <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">\n190\t            <ResponsiveCard className=\"as-section-card\">\n191\t              <div className=\"as-section-head\">\n192\t                <div className=\"as-section-icon blue\"><FaUsers /></div>\n193\t                <span className=\"as-section-title\">Team Members</span>\n194\t                <span className=\"as-section-count\">{team.length} members</span>\n195\t                <div className=\"as-head-actions\">\n196\t                  <ResponsiveButton variant=\"outline-secondary\" size=\"sm\" className=\"as-btn add\" onClick={fetchTeam} title=\"Refresh\">\n197\t                    <FaSync />\n198\t                  </ResponsiveButton>\n199\t                  <ResponsiveButton variant=\"primary\" size=\"sm\" className=\"as-btn add\" onClick={openTmAdd}>\n200\t                    <FaPlus />Add Member\n201\t                  </ResponsiveButton>\n202\t                </div>\n203\t              </div>\n204\t              <div className=\"as-section-body\">\n205\t                <ResponsiveAlert show={!!alert.team?.msg} onHide={() => clearAlert('team')} message={alert.team?.msg} type={alert.team?.type} />\n206\t                {loading.team ? (\n207\t                  <div className=\"as-loading\"><div className=