.. team members content ...\\n\\nBut looking at the end of the file, after the Timeline card closes, I see:\\n```\\n              </ResponsiveCard>\\n            </div>  <!-- This closes the Timeline column -->\\n\\n            {/* \u2500\u2500 Team Members \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */}\\n            <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">  <!-- This opens the Team Members column -->\\n              <ResponsiveCard className=\"as-section-card\">\\n                ... team members content ...\\n              </ResponsiveCard>\\n            </div>  <!-- This should close the Team Members column -->\\n          </div>  <!-- This closes the as-section-row -->\\n        </div>  <!-- This closes the as-page -->\\n      </PageShell>\\n```\\n\\nBut in the current code, after the Team Members ResponsiveCard closes, I see:\\n```\\n              </ResponsiveCard>\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n      </PageShell>\\n```\\n\\nSo there\\'s an extra `</div>` that\\'s causing the adjacent JSX elements error. Let me trace this:\\n\\nFrom line 239-245:\\n```\\n              </ResponsiveCard>\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n      </PageShell>\\n```\\n\\nThis suggests that after the Team Members ResponsiveCard closes, we have:\\n1. `</div>` (line 240) - closes the Team Members column\\n2. `</div>` (line 241) - closes the as-section-row  \\n3. `</div>` (line 242) - closes the as-page\\n4. `</PageShell>` (line 243-244)\\n\\nBut looking at the opening structure, we should have:\\n1. `<PageShell>` \\n2. `<div className=\"as-page\">`\\n3. `<div className=\"as-section-row row g-4\">`\\n4. `<div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">` (Timeline column)\\n5. `<ResponsiveCard className=\"as-section-card\">` (Timeline card)\\n6. ... timeline content ...\\n7. `</ResponsiveCard>` (end Timeline card)\\n8. `</div>` (end Timeline column)\\n9. `<div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">` (Team Members column) \\n10. `<ResponsiveCard className=\"as-section-card\">` (Team Members card)\\n11. ... team members content ...\\n12. `</ResponsiveCard>` (end Team Members card)\\n13. `</div>` (end Team Members column)\\n14. `</div>` (end as-section-row)\\n15. `</div>` (end as-page)\\n16. `</PageShell>`\\n\\nSo we\\'re missing the opening `<div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">` for the Team Members column! Let me check where that should be.\\n\\nLooking at lines 188-189:\\n```\\n          {/* \u2500\u2500 Team Members \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */}\\n          <div className=\"col-12 col-sm-6\">\\n```\\n\\nAh, there it is! So the Team Members column opens at line 189. Then the ResponsiveCard opens at line 190. The content goes through, and then at the end we should close the ResponsiveCard, then close the column div.\\n\\nBut looking at the end of the file, after the Team Members ResponsiveCard content, I see:\\n```\\n              </ResponsiveCard>\\n            </div>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n      </PageShell>\\n```\\n\\nSo:\\n- Line 240: `</ResponsiveCard>` (closes Team Members card)\\n- Line 241: `</div>` (closes Team Members column)  \\n- Line 242: `</div>` (closes as-section-row)\\n- Line 243: `</div>` (closes as-page)\\n- Line 244-245: `</PageShell>`\\n\\nThat looks correct! So why the error?\\n\\nLet me look more carefully at the exact lines around 240. The error says line 240:14. Let me see what\\'s at that position.\\n\\nActually, let me check if there\\'s a missing opening div somewhere. Looking at the structure again...\\n\\nWait, I think I see it. Let me look at the very end of the file as shown in the Read output:\\n\\n```\\n240              </ResponsiveCard>\\n241            </div>\\n242          </div>\\n243        </div>\\n244      </PageShell>\\n245\\t};\\n246\\t\\n247\\texport default AdminSettings;\\n248\\t\\n```\\n\\nSo lines 240-244 are:\\n240: `              </ResponsiveCard>`\\n241: `            </div>`\\n242: `          </div>` \\n243: `        </div>`\\n244: `      </PageShell>`\\n\\nBut we should have:\\n240: `              </ResponsiveCard>`\\n241: `            </div>`  // closes Team Members column\\n242: `          </div>`  // closes as-section-row\\n243: `        </div>`   // closes as-page\\n244: `      </PageShell>`\\n\\nThat looks right. But the error says \"Adjacent JSX elements must be wrapped in an enclosing tag\" at line 240:14.\\n\\nLet me think about what JSX elements are adjacent at that point. At line 240, we have the closing `</ResponsiveCard>` tag. What comes before it? The last element of the Team Members card content.\\n\\nLooking at lines 232-238:\\n```\\n                        {m.bio && (\\n                          <div className=\"as-entry-body\">\\n                            <p style={{ margin: 0, fontSize: \\'.875rem\\', color: \\'#6b7280\\' }}>{m.bio}</p>\\n                          </div>\\n                        )}\\n                      </div>\\n                    ))}\\n```\\n\\nSo the last thing rendered in the map is a closing `</div>` (line 236), then another `</div>` (line 237), then another `</div>` (line 238) which closes the map iterator, then we have the closing `</div>` for the as-entries (line 239), then the closing `</ResponsiveCard>` (line 240).\\n\\nActually, let me look at this more carefully. The structure is:\\n```\\n                  <div className=\"as-entries\">\\n                    {team.map((m, idx) => (\\n                      <div className=\"as-entry-card\" key={m.id || idx}>\\n                        ... entry content ...\\n                      </div>\\n                    ))}\\n                  </div>\\n```\\n\\nSo:\\n- Line 232: `                  <div className=\"as-entries\">`\\n- Line 233: `                    {team.map((m, idx) => (`\\n- Line 234-238: The entry card content\\n- Line 239: `                    ))}` (this closes the map)\\n- Line 240: `                  </div>` (this should close the as-entries div)\\n- Line 241: `                </div>` (this should close the as-section-body)\\n- Line 242: `              </ResponsiveCard>` (this should close the ResponsiveCard)\\n- Line 243: `            </div>` (this should close the Team Members column)\\n- Line 244: `          </div>` (this should close the as-section-row)\\n- Line 245: `        </div>` (this should close the as-page)\\n- Line 246: `      </PageShell>` (this should close the PageShell)\\n\\nBut in the actual code I\\'m seeing:\\n```\\n239                </div>\\n240              </ResponsiveCard>\\n241            </div>\\n242          </div>\\n243        </div>\\n244      </PageShell\\n```\\n\\nSo:\\n- Line 239: `                </div>` (closes as-entries)  \\n- Line 240: `              </ResponsiveCard>` (closes ResponsiveCard)\\n- Line 241: `            </div>` (closes as-section-body)\\n- Line 242: `          </div>` (closes Team Members column)\\n- Line 243: `        </div>` (closes as-section-row)\\n- Line 244: `      </PageShell>` (closes as-page)\\n\\nAh! I see the issue now. The closing tags are mismatched. We have:\\n\\n1. Line 239: Closes the `as-entries` div\\n2. Line 240: Should close the `as-section-body` div, but instead closes the `ResponsiveCard`  \\n3. Line 241: Should close the `ResponsiveCard`, but instead closes the `as-section-body` div\\n4. Line 242: Should close the Team Members column div, but instead closes the as-section-row div\\n5. Line 243: Should close the as-section-row div, but instead closes the as-page div\\n6. Line 244: Should close the as-page div, but instead closes the PageShell\\n\\nThe problem is that the closing `</ResponsiveCard>` tag is in the wrong place. It should come after the closing `</div>` for the as-section-body, not before it.\\n\\nLooking at the structure, it should be:\\n```\\n                  <div className=\"as-entries\">\\n                    {team.map(...)}\\n                  </div>\\n                </div>  <!-- as-section-body -->\\n              </ResponsiveCard>\\n            </div>  <!-- Team Members column -->\\n          </div>  <!-- as-section-row -->\\n        </div>  <!-- as-page -->\\n      </PageShell>\\n```\\n\\nBut we have:\\n```\\n                  <div className=\"as-entries\">\\n                    {team.map(...)}\\n                  </div>\\n              </ResponsiveCard>  <!-- WRONG PLACE -->\\n            </div>  <!-- This is actually closing as-section-body -->\\n          </div>  <!-- This is actually closing Team Members column -->\\n        </div>  <!-- This is actually closing as-section-row -->\\n      </PageShell>  <!-- This is actually closing as-page -->\\n```\\n\\nSo the `</ResponsiveCard>` on line 240 is in the wrong place. It should be moved down to after the `</div>` that closes the as-section-body.\\n\\nLet me find where the as-section-body opening tag is to confirm the structure.\\n\\nLooking backwards from line 239:\\n```\\n204                <div className=\"as-section-body\">\\n205                  <ResponsiveAlert show={!!alert.team?.msg} onHide={() => clearAlert(\\'team\\')} message={alert.team?.msg} type={alert.team?.type} />\\n206                  {loading.team ? (\\n207                    <div className=\"as-loading\"><div className=\"as-spinner\" />Loading team members\u2026</div>\\n208                  ) : team.length === 0 ? (\\n209                    <div className=\"as-empty\">\\n210                      <div className=\"as-empty-icon\"><FaUsers /></div>\\n211                      <div class